\f1\fs22 The sounds of the mansion became familiar to Sarah\'97the murmur of eager tourists; the scuffing of their feet on polished floors; the outbursts of excited, tired children; the rehearsed commentaries of the tour guides\'97which is why Sarah woke up alarmed by their absence. More alarming were the sounds replacing the tourists. To Sarah, it sounded as if the surrounds of the mansion has been converted to a parade ground. She thought she heard marching and someone barking out orders. In fear, she catapulted from her bed as fast as a trebuchet slap\'97bed linen flapping and drifting in her wake\'97and landed harshly by the windows over the portico. Indeed, as Sarah witnessed, a battalion of Elvi in camouflage ponchos were parading on the once-manicured lawns of the mansion.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Halt,\'92 a parade master called from his position under the portico, as the formation came before the front door. \'91Right turn. Present arms.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A battalion of Elvi jumped as one into a wide-footed stance with hands up, as if to perform a cartoonish judo chop.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah could not believe her eyes, or that anything could be more unbelievable. Until the tanks started rolling up the driveway.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A dim part of Sarah\'92s brain begged her to hide under the blankets, even while she threw back the bedroom door, strong-armed Nancy out of her way, descended the staircase and hurled out the door to confront the enemy\'97in a t-shirt and yesterday\'92s underwear.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>His back to her, the parade master barked, \'91
\f2\i Army manual, section 43\'97when in hand to hand combat with the enemy, apply judo chop to the back of neck.
\f1\i0 \'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The battalion executed some judo manoeuvre in rough unison.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What, the tax?\'97who the\'97\'92 Sarah was instantly embarrassed by how erudite she failed to be.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Forgive me ma\'92am. I hope we didn\'92t wake you,\'92 said the parade master, as ranks and file of Elvi stood frozen at ease.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarak blinked, and patted down her t-shirt with one hand while raking her tangled bed hair with the other. \'91Why, um \'85 no \'85\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Allow me to introduce myself, Holy Momma,\'92 the Elvi said. \'91Specialist 5 Tulsa McLean, at your service.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah thighs felt cold; she suppressed the urge to cross her knees. \'91My service?\'92 In spite of the awkwardness, she felt flattered.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We\'92re here for your protection, ma\'92am.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91With tanks?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tulsa chuckled through a lopsided grin. \'91We had a couple of spares, so, why not defend headquarters?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Head \'85 quarters \'85\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tulsa, for the first time, looked beyond Sarah\'92s eyes and noticed the gooseflesh on her arms and legs. \'91Forgive me ma\'92am. You\'92re freezing out here.\'92 He guided her, confused and compliant, inside.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>In the lobby, Sarah regathered her wits. \'91You have more tanks?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yes we do, ma\'92am.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah worked her jaw and her eyes darted about as she processed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Best if you don\'92t worry about any of this. We\'92re looking after you and everyone you care about,\'92 Tulsa said, flashing a glance at Sarah\'92s tummy.
